\":1183,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":53376,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1183,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FX5tNdu2GdQj8RAWQjKBx5\",\"session_id\":\"c85b8a49-1fe0-40b1-a281-e4278d224d69\",\"uuid\":\"f1d8c8b0-e537-483e-84b5-6d21ee772b53\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-06T21:11:43.048Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfmftZYE3wbzuia2YJkem\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"task_description\":\"Adversarial code audit variant a\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\",\"task_id\":\"bv02db77u\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AbYU3jwzfQp3sW9jUdMJaj\",\"description\":\"Run the template's jest tests\",\"is_backgrounded\":false,\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"uuid\":\"1a0476e2-2db8-4286-aee3-4b3b7b2af7ff\",\"session_id\":\"c85b8a49-1fe0-40b1-a281-e4278d224d69\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfmftZpLhXHZbRwbfrmsb\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I found no confirmed defects that break the brief. There are three small deviations and two places where the contract checks less than the brief promises. I edited nothing in the repo; one scratch probe is at `C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic-production\\\\one-a-day\\\\journal\\\\2026-10-06\\\\critique-scratch\\\\probe.cjs`. The probe ran against the uncommitted, since-modified `dist` build, not `src`.\\n\\n**Minor deviations from the brief (all in `src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts`)**\\n1. **Accent contrast (L320):** the code checks hero-number contrast against `TILE` (#fbfbfb). The brief says \\\"against the page\\\" (`PAPER` #f6f4ee). The numbers do sit on tiles, but an accent between about 4.3:1 and 4.5:1 against the page passes here and would fail the brief's wording.\\n2. **Event name fit (L120, `nameLines`):** a long name shrinks to 70% and then wraps to two lines. The brief says \\\"shrink to 70%, then refuse\\\". The contract follows the two-line version (L845, `event-name-1`).\\n3. **Milestones parsing (L218, L222):**\\n   - Text with no entries, such as `\\\",,,\\\"`, silently shows the empty-week line.\\n   - `\\\"4xR025\\\"` is read as R25 and `\\\"001xR25\\\"` as 1 runner.\\n   - None of these produces a wrong number, but none is refused either.\\n\\n**Contract gaps (L841-860)**\\n- The brief promises exactly 2 hero tiles and exactly 4 stat tiles. Neither the layout constraints nor the equal-size relations can count, so the contract can't hold that. The test covers it only through the value text sizes (test L120-121), not the tile rects.\\n- Each tile label has no presence entry of its own. Only `value-*` has one (L850). The fit check (L819) covers them only indirectly.\\n\\n**Checked and fine**\\n- **Defaults (L82-92):** every prop has a default and all match the brief's table.\\n- **Determinism:** no `Date`, `Math.random` or clock calls. The weekday comes from the date string with Sakamoto's method (L209-211). The probe got 2026-10-03 SAT, 2024-02-29 THU, 2000-01-01 SAT, 2000-02-29 TUE and 1900-01-01 MON. 1900-02-29 and 2100-02-29 are refused, and the leap-year rule is right (L205).\\n- **Number format (L195):** 1000 prints as 1,000, 1204 as 1,204 and 9999 as 9,999. There is no \\\"k\\\".\\n- **Refusals:** each one names the field and value. Covered: unknown key (L246), missing key (L250), new PBs over finishers (L257), first-time volunteers over volunteers (L259), R30 (L225), duplicate R25 (L228), 11 entries (L219) and a bad date (L303). Negative numbers, 3.5, NaN and 10000 are refused (L252), as are run numbers 0 and 10000 (L299), `0xR25` (L226), `1000xR25` and a bare `R25` (L223), and unknown props, with a \\\"did you mean\\\" suggestion (L292).\\n- **Contract values:** the header band [0, 0.25], footer [0.9, 1], hero position [0.1, 0.8] and stat `minWidthFrac` 0.15 match the brief. So do the band's [0.55, 1] with 0.85, size tolerance 2, and badges kept equal and inside the band. Nothing was widened.\\n- **Tests:** none is tautological, and every loop runs over a non-empty set. Two are weak but valid: the determinism test (L258) compares two separate renders, and L232 only checks that the render succeeds.\\n- **Non-ASCII:** found in comments (L177, 324, 425, 449, 518, 580, 656), in the font-range regex (L182), and in the label's \\\"·\\\" (L767). None of it is drawn on the card. All 18 templates in the repo use the same pattern, and AGENTS.md only requires ASCII in rendered copy. The test enforces that for the default card (L55).\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1183,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":53376,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1183,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FX5tNdu2GdQj8RAWQjKBx5\",\"session_id\":\"c85b8a49-1fe0-40b1-a281-e4278d224d69\",\"uuid\":\"3b8e3432-3456-417d-a60f-62786d606e3a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-06T21:11:48.582Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfmftZYE3wbzuia2YJkem\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"task_description\":\"Adversarial code audit variant a\"}","+[14:11:48] critique-2   └─ 💬 I found no confirmed defects that break the brief. There are three small deviations and two places where the contract checks less than the brief promises. I edited nothing in the repo; one scratch probe is at `C:\\src\\m0s","+{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",\"rate_limit_info\":{\"status\":\"allowed\",\"resetsAt\":1791336600,\"rateLimitType\":\"five_hour\",\"overageStatus\":\"rejected\",\"overageDisabledReason\":\"org_level_disabled\",\"isUsingOverage\":false,